State delta:
- LOCAL only: `public.apply_meeting_note_ai_draft(p_note_id, p_expected_revision, p_summary, p_items jsonb)` 
(authenticated SECURITY DEFINER; validates, locks via `private.meeting_note_lock_for_change`, requires editor rights + 
draft source revision, current-member assignees, appends items (capacity trigger rolls back all), writes summary (NULL 
keeps current summary/generator), `generated_by='ai'` only when summary written, revision +1, one version; existing 
items untouched) → {note_id, revision, version_id, item_ids, duplicate_indexes}.
- `POST /api/meeting-notes/[id]/ai/process` {ticket, idempotencyKey?}: origin guard + auth → rate limit 
`meeting-note:ai-process` 20/60 s → ticket signature/expiry → binding (user ≠ 409, company ≠ 404, note/key mismatch 
409) → service-role admission (actor = dbUser.id) → normalize → preflight → mark dispatched → adapter (request.signal 
+ timeout, default 180 s, optional `MEETING_NOTES_AI_TIMEOUT_MS`) → membership/editor/note recheck → settle. 200 
{operationId, status, replay, sourceRevision, transcriptId, draft|null, usage|null}; replay = status only. Errors: 400 
TICKET_INVALID, 410 TICKET_EXPIRED, 409 BINDING_MISMATCH / NOT_CONFIGURED / SETTINGS_STALE {settings} / SOURCE_STALE / 
OPERATION_ENDED / DRAFT_DISCARDED, 429 LIMIT_REACHED {limit, used, usageDay, resetAt}, 404/403 (also when access lost 
while processing → discarded), 422 TRANSCRIPT_TOO_LONG_FOR_MODEL (released), 502 adapter failure, 499 CANCELLED, 503 
UNAVAILABLE. Never the key, transcript, or provider text.
- Settlement: preflight refusal / client gone before mark → released; success with client present + rights + note → 
succeeded; success but client left or access lost → discarded; processed_failure → failed (discarded if client left); 
preprocessing_rejected → refunded; never_sent after mark → refunded; unexpected error before mark → released (refunded 
if mark committed); after mark → failed; settle changed=false/other status → draft dropped.
- Name resolution (`src/lib/meeting-notes/ai/draft-review.ts`): NFD/unaccented/lower/trimmed/collapsed; unique exact 
full name → member; else unique first name → member; else unassigned; duplicate marking against existing items.
- Summary stored as plain text: "Key points" / "Decisions" / "Next steps" headings with "- entry" lines; all empty → 
NULL (keeps current).
- `POST /api/meeting-notes/[id]/ai/apply` {expectedRevision, summary{…}, items[{description, assigneeId?, dueDate?}]} 
→ 200 {note, applied}; 409 STALE with current note; explicit duplicates allowed and reported.
- Child-process harness `__tests__/meeting-notes-db/child/{start-route-child.mjs, next-headers-shim.mjs}` (jiti) for 
crash/restart/production cases; `route-session.ts` snapshots cookies per request and supports AbortSignal.
